{
  "description": "Failure isolation for one peer device. Input per case: the device's cursor (known), the raw marker text (headText, null when absent), the raw journal text as downloaded (journalText, null when the file is gone) and the journal size the directory listing reported (listedBytes, null when unknown). expected.fetch says whether the journal is downloaded at all (a caught-up reader skips it unless the listed size is below the marker's journalBytes). expected.blocked is null or one of head-corrupt | journal-corrupt | journal-truncated | journal-missing; a blocked device never fails the pull for other devices. expected.seqs are the records still exposed (a truncated journal exposes its complete committed rows). reset follows committed-view.json. Only the codes are contract; messages are local. Network, authentication and server errors are not isolated: they fail the whole pull.",
